---
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout title="Terms of Use" description={`The terms that apply when you use ${SITE.name}'s free finance calculators and guides.`} updated="October 2026">
  <p>By using {SITE.domain} you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.</p>

  <h2>Educational use only</h2>
  <p>
    Our calculators and guides are general information to help you understand money decisions. They are not financial,
    tax, legal or investment advice, and they don't take your personal circumstances into account. See our
    <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to keep every calculator correct and up to date, but we can't guarantee that results are free of
    errors or that rules haven't changed since our last update. Results are estimates. Always confirm figures with
    your lender, the relevant government body or a qualified adviser before you act.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You may use the calculators for personal, non-commercial purposes free of charge.</li>
    <li>You may link to any page on the site.</li>
    <li>You may not copy the site's content or code for republication, or scrape it automatically, without permission.</li>
    <li>You may not use the site in a way that harms it or other users.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    We link to official sources and, sometimes, to other companies. We aren't responsible for the content of other
    websites, and a link isn't an endorsement unless we say so.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} is not liable for any loss arising from your use of the site or
    reliance on its results. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
